 {"id": "PEDS-U383", "ch": 48, "n": 1, "title": "Neuroblastoma — Origin, Pathology & Clinical Features", "sec": "Neuroblastoma features and pathology · p223", "guide": "Neuroblastoma is the m/c intra-abdominal tumour, the m/c extra-cranial solid tumour and the 2nd m/c solid tumour (after intracranial/brain tumours) of children — and the m/c malignancy of infancy. It arises from neuroblasts (neural crest cells), most often in the adrenal gland (suprarenal tumour), then the paravertebral sympathetic chain/ganglia, posterior mediastinum and pelvis. Microscopy: small round uniform blue cells with scanty cytoplasm and hyperchromatic nuclei forming Homer-Wright rosettes with central eosinophilic neuropil (cytoplasmic processes). Features: firm fixed irregular midline abdominal mass, constitutional symptoms, Horner syndrome and heterochromia iridis; metastases to bone (m/c → bony pain), retro-orbital region (raccoon eyes) and skin (blueberry muffin lesions).", "qs": ["PEDS-C48-001", "PEDS-C48-002", "PEDS-C48-003", "PEDS-C48-004", "PEDS-C48-005", "PEDS-C48-006", "PEDS-C48-007", "PEDS-C48-008", "PEDS-C48-009", "PEDS-C48-010", "PEDS-C48-011", "PEDS-C48-012", "PEDS-C48-013", "PEDS-C48-014", "PEDS-C48-015", "PEDS-C48-016", "PEDS-C48-017", "PEDS-C48-018", "PEDS-C48-019", "PEDS-C48-020", "PEDS-C48-021", "PEDS-C48-022", "PEDS-C48-023", "PEDS-C48-024", "PEDS-C48-025", "PEDS-C48-026", "PEDS-C48-027", "PEDS-C48-028", "PEDS-C48-029"]},
 {"id": "PEDS-U384", "ch": 48, "n": 2, "title": "Neuroblastoma — Paraneoplastic Effects, Investigations, Staging & Treatment", "sec": "Neuroblastoma work-up and management · p223–224", "guide": "Paraneoplastic: opsoclonus-myoclonus ataxia (dancing eye/dancing feet syndrome, anti-neuronal antibodies) and VIP hypersecretion → intractable watery diarrhea with hypokalemia. Investigations: urine catecholamine metabolites VMA and HVA (initial, non-specific), NSE (most specific); CT abdomen (m/c) shows stippled calcifications and a mass displacing the kidney inferolaterally (unlike Wilms); I¹²³ MIBG and PET-CT rule out metastases. INSS stages I, 2 (2a/2b), 3 (crosses midline or contralateral nodes), 4 (disseminated), 4S (infant, good prognosis). Low risk: stages I, II, 4s, onset < 18 months, hyperdiploidy, TRK A expression; high risk: stages 3/4, onset > 18 months, hypodiploidy, N-myc amplification, loss of heterozygosity (1p, 11q). Treatment: localised → resection; disseminated → surgery + cisplatin, cyclophosphamide, vincristine, etoposide; no response → radiotherapy; refractory → autologous HSCT.", "qs": ["PEDS-C48-030", "PEDS-C48-031", "PEDS-C48-032", "PEDS-C48-033", "PEDS-C48-034", "PEDS-C48-035", "PEDS-C48-036", "PEDS-C48-037", "PEDS-C48-038", "PEDS-C48-039", "PEDS-C48-040", "PEDS-C48-041", "PEDS-C48-042", "PEDS-C48-043", "PEDS-C48-044", "PEDS-C48-045", "PEDS-C48-046", "PEDS-C48-047", "PEDS-C48-048", "PEDS-C48-049", "PEDS-C48-050", "PEDS-C48-051", "PEDS-C48-052", "PEDS-C48-053", "PEDS-C48-054", "PEDS-C48-055", "PEDS-C48-056", "PEDS-C48-057", "PEDS-C48-058", "PEDS-C48-059", "PEDS-C48-060", "PEDS-C48-061", "PEDS-C48-062", "PEDS-C48-063", "PEDS-C48-064", "PEDS-C48-065", "PEDS-C48-066", "PEDS-C48-067"]},
 {"id": "PEDS-U385", "ch": 48, "n": 3, "title": "Wilms Tumour — Features, Associations & Clinical Picture", "sec": "Wilms tumour features and associations · p224", "guide": "Wilms tumour (nephroblastoma) is the m/c solid tumour of the kidney in childhood and the 2nd m/c intra-abdominal tumour; usually unilateral. Cell of origin: nephrogenic rest (undifferentiated mesenchyme of the kidney); age 2–5 years. Risk factors: horseshoe kidney (4× risk), cryptorchidism and hypospadias. WT-1 (11p13) mutation → WAGR (Wilms tumour, Aniridia, Genitourinary anomalies, mental Retardation) and Denys-Drash syndrome (diffuse mesangial sclerosis → congenital nephrotic syndrome; ambiguous genitalia in males). WT-2 (11p15) mutation → Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome (LGA with hemihypertrophy, macroglossia, omphalocele, organomegaly, ear lobe creases). Clinical: asymptomatic loin mass, hypertension from ↑ renin, hematuria. Metastasis: lung (m/c) > lymph node > liver.", "qs": ["PEDS-C48-068", "PEDS-C48-069", "PEDS-C48-070", "PEDS-C48-071", "PEDS-C48-072", "PEDS-C48-073", "PEDS-C48-074", "PEDS-C48-075", "PEDS-C48-076", "PEDS-C48-077", "PEDS-C48-078", "PEDS-C48-079", "PEDS-C48-080", "PEDS-C48-081", "PEDS-C48-082", "PEDS-C48-083", "PEDS-C48-084", "PEDS-C48-085", "PEDS-C48-086", "PEDS-C48-087", "PEDS-C48-088", "PEDS-C48-089", "PEDS-C48-090", "PEDS-C48-091", "PEDS-C48-092", "PEDS-C48-093"]},
 {"id": "PEDS-U386", "ch": 48, "n": 4, "title": "Wilms Tumour — COG Staging & Treatment", "sec": "Wilms tumour staging and treatment · p225", "guide": "Children's Oncology Group (COG) staging is POST-SURGICAL: stage 1 confined to kidney and completely resectable; stage 2 extends outside the kidney but completely resectable with uninvolved nodes; stage 3 residual tumour confined to abdomen, regional node metastasis or tumour extension into IVC; stage 4 nodal metastasis outside the abdomen or hematogenous metastasis to organs like lung and liver; stage 5 bilateral kidney involvement. Treatment: radical nephrectomy for stages 1–4 — stages 1/2 get vincristine + actinomycin D for 18 weeks; stages 3/4 get vincristine + actinomycin D + doxorubicin for 24 weeks AND radiotherapy. Partial nephrectomy for stage 5, with surgery + chemotherapy + radiotherapy.", "qs": ["PEDS-C48-094", "PEDS-C48-095", "PEDS-C48-096", "PEDS-C48-097", "PEDS-C48-098", "PEDS-C48-099", "PEDS-C48-100", "PEDS-C48-101", "PEDS-C48-102", "PEDS-C48-103", "PEDS-C48-104", "PEDS-C48-105", "PEDS-C48-106", "PEDS-C48-107", "PEDS-C48-108", "PEDS-C48-109", "PEDS-C48-110", "PEDS-C48-111", "PEDS-C48-112", "PEDS-C48-113", "PEDS-C48-114", "PEDS-C48-115"]},
