 {"sec": "Neuroblastoma work-up and management · p223–224", "page": 223, "q": "Stage 3 neuroblastoma is defined by a tumour that —", "opts": ["Is disseminated", "Shows bone metastasis in an infant", "Crosses the midline or has contralateral nodes", "Is completely resectable"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Stage 3: crosses the midline OR unilateral tumour + contralateral LN involvement. (Book p223)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C48-046"},
 {"sec": "Neuroblastoma work-up and management · p223–224", "page": 223, "q": "Stage 4 neuroblastoma is characterised by —", "opts": ["Tumour crossing the midline", "No node involvement", "Bilateral kidney involvement", "Disseminated tumour"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Stage 4: disseminated tumours. (Book p223)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C48-047"},
 {"sec": "Neuroblastoma work-up and management · p223–224", "page": 223, "q": "Stage 4S neuroblastoma refers to a stage I tumour or a tumour with dissemination to bone/liver/skin in ___.", "opts": ["An infant", "A child over 5 years", "An adolescent", "A newborn with bone marrow disease"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Stage 4S: stage I or a tumour with dissemination to bone/liver/skin, in an infant — with good prognosis. (Book p223)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C48-048"},
 {"sec": "Neuroblastoma work-up and management · p223–224", "page": 223, "q": "The prognostic significance of stage 4S neuroblastoma is —", "opts": ["Requires radiotherapy regardless", "Good prognosis", "Worst prognosis", "Same as stage 4"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Stage 4S carries a good prognosis. (Book p223)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C48-049"},
 {"sec": "Neuroblastoma work-up and management · p223–224", "page": 223, "q": "A 4-month-old infant has a small adrenal neuroblastoma with liver and skin nodules.", "opts": ["Stage 3 — high risk", "Wilms tumour stage 5", "Stage 4S — good prognosis", "Stage 4 — poor prognosis"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Dissemination to bone/liver/skin in an infant with stage I disease defines stage 4S, which has a good prognosis. (Book p223)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 4-month-old infant has a small adrenal neuroblastoma with liver and skin deposits but no bone marrow involvement.", "id": "PEDS-C48-050"},
 {"sec": "Neuroblastoma work-up and management · p223–224", "page": 223, "q": "True or False — In neuroblastoma, the contrast CT shows stippled calcifications and inferolateral displacement of the kidney, unlike Wilms tumour.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — these CT features (specifically the inferolateral displacement) are not seen in Wilms tumour. (Book p223)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C48-051"},
 {"sec": "Neuroblastoma work-up and management · p223–224", "page": 223, "q": "True or False — The catecholamine metabolites VMA and HVA are highly specific for neuroblastoma.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — they are non-specific; NSE is the most specific marker. (Book p223)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C48-052"},
 {"sec": "Neuroblastoma work-up and management · p223–224", "page": 223, "q": "Odd one out (paraneoplastic/manifestation features described for neuroblastoma):", "opts": ["Heterochromia iridis", "Flushing with hypertension from catecholamine excess", "Opsoclonus-myoclonus ataxia", "Intractable watery diarrhea with hypokalemia"], "ans": 1, "exp": "The chapter's paraneoplastic list is opsoclonus-myoclonus ataxia and VIP hypersecretion; heterochromia iridis is a direct tumour feature and flushing from catecholamines is not described. (Book p223)", "type": "odd", "id": "PEDS-C48-053"},
 {"sec": "Neuroblastoma work-up and management · p223–224", "page": 224, "q": "The low-risk group of neuroblastoma includes stages I, II and ___.", "opts": ["4", "2b only", "4s", "3"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Low risk: stage I, II, 4s; age < 18 months; hyperdiploidy and TRK A gene expression. (Book p224)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C48-054"},
 {"sec": "Neuroblastoma work-up and management · p223–224", "page": 224, "q": "Regarding the age of onset, low-risk neuroblastoma is < ___ months and high risk > ___ months.", "opts": ["12; 12", "24; 24", "6; 6", "18; 18"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Risk table: age of onset < 18 months = low risk; > 18 months = high risk. (Book p224)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C48-055"},
 {"sec": "Neuroblastoma work-up and management · p223–224", "page": 224, "q": "Which genetic feature places a neuroblastoma in the low-risk group?", "opts": ["Hyperdiploidy", "Hypodiploidy", "N-myc amplification", "Loss of heterozygosity"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Low risk genetics: hyperdiploidy and TRK A gene expression. (Book p224)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C48-056"},
